<script>
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import CornerGrip from './lib/CornerGrip.abide'
import cornerGrip from './lib/CornerGrip.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import EdgeDragged from './lib/EdgeDragged.abide'
import edgeDragged from './lib/EdgeDragged.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import RightPanel from './lib/RightPanel.abide'
import rightPanel from './lib/RightPanel.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import Sidebar from './lib/Sidebar.abide'
import sidebar from './lib/Sidebar.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/behaviors/element-size', '/headless/dialog']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealSplit.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the deal list sizes from its handle, within its bounds'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/resizable.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the panel keeps to min, max and what its parent leaves after keep",
                "test('the arrows of its own axis step it",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Size a sidebar by dragging its edge">
        <p>Spread <code>panel</code> on the panel and <code>handle</code> on the edge between it
            and its neighbour. The panel keeps to <code>min</code> and <code>max</code>, and, given
            <code>keep</code>, to its parent's room less the pixels left to what stands beside
            it.
            The arrow keys step it, Home and End take it to its bounds, Enter collapses it and
            restores it, and a double click gives it back its own size.</p>
        <Example code={sidebar}><Sidebar /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Size a panel on the right from its left edge">
        <p>Give <code>edge: 'start'</code> where the handle stands before the panel: moving it
            left grows the panel. Hand in <code>size</code> to keep it, in a store or anywhere
            else.</p>
        <Example code={rightPanel}><RightPanel /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Size a box from its corner">
        <p>One <code>resizable</code> per axis, both handles spread on one grip. A drag moves
            each along its own axis, and each answers only the arrow keys of its own. With no
            <code>keep</code>, the box its height sizes grows with it rather than bounding
            it.</p>
        <Example code={cornerGrip}><CornerGrip /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Color the edge while it is dragged">
        <p>The handle carries <code>data-dragging</code> from the press to the release.</p>
        <Example code={edgeDragged}><EdgeDragged /></Example>
    </Section>
</Doc>
